{"id":"2c5cf6deb9c2688f2458afd06ef1b27cc1232a40","axis":"silent","repo":"grafana/tempo","sha":"2c5cf6deb9c2688f2458afd06ef1b27cc1232a40","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".chloggen/query-frontend-job-metrics.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@","+change_type: enhancement","+","+component: query-frontend","+","+note: Add `tempo_query_frontend_job_inspected_bytes`, a histogram of the bytes inspected by each querier job per operation, and `tempo_query_frontend_executing_jobs`, a gauge of the jobs currently executing on queriers per tenant and operation","+","+issues: []","+","+subtext:","+","+user: stoewer"],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".chloggen/trace-by-id-inspected-bytes.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@","+change_type: change","+","+component: query-frontend","+","+note: Trace by ID now reports the bytes read from bloom filters and indexes, and the bytes of jobs that find no trace, in `tempo_query_frontend_bytes_inspected_total` and the `inspectedBytes` response metric","+","+issues: []","+","+subtext: |","+  `tempo_query_frontend_bytes_inspected_total{op=\"traces\"}`, `tempo_live_store_query_inspected_bytes_total{op=\"trace_by_id\"}` and the `inspected_bytes` field of the trace by ID response log increase, in some cases considerably.","+  The throughput that trace by ID requests are compared with `throughput_bytes_slo` rises as well.","+  Dashboards, alerts, SLOs and autoscaling rules based on these values, such as querier autoscaling on the bytes inspected rate, may need to be adjusted.","+","+user: stoewer"],"additions":14,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"cmd/tempo-cli/cmd-rewrite-blocks.go","lines":["@@ -253,7 +253,8 @@ func isInBlock(ctx context.Context, r backend.Reader, background bool, blockNum"," \t\t\treturn nil, err"," \t\t}"," ","-\t\tif trace == nil {","+\t\t// blocks ruled out by the bloom filter or index respond without a trace","+\t\tif trace.GetTrace() == nil {"," \t\t\tcontinue"," \t\t}"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"cmd/tempo-cli/cmd-rewrite-blocks_test.go","lines":["@@ -203,3 +203,49 @@ func (i *testIterator) Next(context.Context) (common.ID, *tempopb.Trace, error)"," "," func (i *testIterator) Close() {"," }","+","+// Blocks that are ruled out by the bloom filter must not be reported as containing a trace.","+func TestIsInBlock(t *testing.T) {","+\tconst (","+\t\ttenantID = \"single-tenant\"","+\t\tblocks   = 3","+\t)","+","+\tdir := t.TempDir()","+\tgenerateTestBlocks(t, dir, tenantID, blocks, 5)","+","+\trawR, _, _, err := local.New(&local.Config{Path: dir})","+\trequire.NoError(t, err)","+\treader := backend.NewReader(rawR)","+\tctx := context.Background()","+","+\tblockIDs, _, _, err := reader.Blocks(ctx, tenantID)","+\trequire.NoError(t, err)","+\trequire.Len(t, blockIDs, blocks)","+","+\t// blocksContaining returns the blocks that report to contain at least one of the IDs","+\tblocksContaining := func(traceIDs ...common.ID) []uuid.UUID {","+\t\tvar found []uuid.UUID","+\t\tfor i, blockID := range blockIDs {","+\t\t\tmeta, err := isInBlock(ctx, reader, true, i, blockID, tenantID, traceIDs...)","+\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)","+\t\t\tif meta != nil {","+\t\t\t\tfound = append(found, uuid.UUID(meta.BlockID))","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t}","+\t\treturn found","+\t}","+","+\tt.Run(\"trace in one block\", func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\tfor _, hexID := range getAllTraceIDs(t, dir, tenantID) {","+\t\t\tid, err := util.HexStringToTraceID(hexID)","+\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)","+","+\t\t\trequire.Len(t, blocksContaining(id), 1, hexID)","+\t\t}","+\t})","+","+\tt.Run(\"trace in no block\", func(t *testing.T) {","+\t\trequire.Empty(t, blocksContaining(test.ValidTraceID(nil)))","+\t})","+}"],"additions":46,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/sources/tempo/operations/monitor/query-io-and-timestamp-distance.md","lines":["@@ -29,8 +29,8 @@ The distributor emits `tempo_spans_distance_in_future_seconds` and `tempo_spans_"," "," | Names | Type | Labels | Buckets | Emitted | Notes |"," |---|---|---|---|---|---|","-| `tempo_query_frontend_bytes_inspected_total` | Counter | `tenant`, `op` | - | As each querier job response is combined at the query frontend; aggregates bytes inspected by the query path, including requests that later fail or are canceled; excludes cached querier responses. | Includes TraceQL metrics queries with `op=\"metrics\"`. |","-| `tempo_live_store_query_inspected_bytes_total` | Counter | `tenant`, `op` | - | During live-store query execution. | Live-store `op` values are `search`, `search_tags`, `search_tag_values`, `trace_by_id`, and `query_range`. |","+| `tempo_query_frontend_bytes_inspected_total` | Counter | `tenant`, `op` | - | As each querier job response is combined at the query frontend; aggregates bytes inspected by the query path, including requests that later fail or are canceled; excludes cached querier responses. | Includes TraceQL metrics queries with `op=\"metrics\"`. For `op=\"traces\"`, includes the bytes read from bloom filters and indexes, also for blocks that don't contain the trace. |","+| `tempo_live_store_query_inspected_bytes_total` | Counter | `tenant`, `op` | - | During live-store query execution. | Live-store `op` values are `search`, `search_tags`, `search_tag_values`, `trace_by_id`, and `query_range`. For `op=\"trace_by_id\"`, includes the bytes read from bloom filters and indexes of complete blocks, also for blocks that don't contain the trace. |"," | `tempo_spans_distance_in_future_seconds`, `tempo_spans_distance_in_past_seconds` | Histogram | `tenant` | 300s, 1800s, 3600s (5m, 30m, 1h) | In the distributor on ingest; observes seconds between span end time and ingestion time. | Spans in the future are accepted but invalid and might not be searchable. |"," "," ## PromQL examples"],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/sources/tempo/reference-tempo-architecture/components/query-frontend.md","lines":["@@ -126,6 +126,8 @@ Refer to [Tune search performan